      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Jared, can you help me understand what factors determine whether `android-platform-build` should be set? Is it the `min_sdk_version` property of the Soong module or the `sdk_version` the Soong module builds against?\n\nAs an example, let us consider the android_test `MtsTetheringTestLatestSdk`. Its Android.bp file looks something like (some parts skipped for brevity)\n```\nandroid_test {\n  name: \"MtsTetheringTestLatestSdk\",\n  min_sdk_version: \"31\",\n  sdk_version: \"core_platform\" # unstable, inherited via defaults\n}\n```\n\nOn ToT, `android-platform-build` is not added to the CLI for this module even though it is building against an unstable api surface (CorePlatformApi). Is this WAI? \n\n(After this CL, this flag will be set.)",
      "parentUuid": "a3815699_944adb8b",
      "revId": "0e40a5135b38555ddd8872ecc643a2dcadc282e2",
