      "message": "Hmm, yeah this case is sort of in a gray area I guess.\n\n@zerny@google.com what would you expect the correct behavior to be for such a target? For tests, there are some cases where we definitely don\u0027t want desugaring (e.g., the libcore tests), but those have been explicitly updated to add the `--android-platform-build` flag (see https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:cts/tests/libcore/luni/Android.bp;drc\u003df467958f5c7933ae633e75d2587b00ffdffd4f8f;l\u003d40). Otherwise, do we need/want to preserve portability at the expense of potential unknown/undefined behavior when building against an unstable API? Does R8 ignore the min-api flag if we also set \u0027--android-platform-build\u0027?",
